# Start the car camera's go2rtc container when a USB camera enumerates.
#
# The container maps the camera with `--device`, and Docker refuses to start
# a container whose device is absent -- a refusal, not a crash, so the
# `--restart unless-stopped` policy never retries it. A camera that is
# missing at boot (an Insta360 X3 that has fallen out of webcam mode, one
# plugged in after the car is on) therefore leaves go2rtc down until someone
# runs `docker start`. This rule is that `docker start`, driven by the event
# that makes it possible: any USB video capture device appearing pulls in
# openlaps-go2rtc.service, a oneshot that starts the container and is a
# no-op when it is already running.
#
# USB only (SUBSYSTEMS/DRIVERS match the parent interface): a Rockchip board
# registers dozens of MIPI video nodes at boot, and none of them is the car
# camera.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", DRIVERS=="uvcvideo", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="openlaps-go2rtc.service"
